<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Bids down on heavy farmer sales.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Bids down on heavy farmer sales.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>A day of heavy farmer sales weakened hard red winter wheat cash basis bids on Tuesday but several merchandisers said movement had slowed considerably since Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We had a pretty good day yesterday but so far today it's pretty quiet,&quot; a central Kansas dealer said.</p>
<p>Active selling on Monday and calls for a lower KCBT opening prompted some locations to take cash protection but there were no reports of protection on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Bids were lower in Salina, Topeka and Colby, Kansas but were a shade higher in Houston.</p>
<p>Several elevators were planning to close early on Tuesday in observance of the New Year's Eve holiday.</p>
